Subscription calculator

For 1 customer
Billing for each customer account
Mlti Currency ? Open
Subsidiaries ? 1 Subsidiaries

Billing Cycle - Weekly/Biweekly/Monthly ? Monthtly and 1st day of month

Do we need Rate limiter ? No


You are a senior software developer and your task is to build a subscription calcuator. Following are the requirements :

1. Billing cycle is monthly, generate bill 1st of every month
2. Data model for calculator input is:
    {
        billing frequecy = "monthly"
        currency = "USD"
        line_items:
            {
                product: "prod1"
                price_model: "flat"
                unit_price: 500
                quantity: 3
                discount {type: "percentage", value: 10}
            }
            {
                product: "prod2"
                price_model: "per_unit"
                unit_price: 0.03
                quantity: 15000
                discount: null
            }
            {
                product: "prod3"
                price_model: "tiered"
                unit_price: 25.00
                quantity: 12
                discount: {type: "fixed", value: 50.00}
            }
    }
3. Write a DTO for this data model that can be used.
4. To calculate billing amount use this formula: amount = Unit price * quanity discount (if type is percentage then calculate the % of unit price * quantity using discont value and then deduct calculated discount from the amount, if type is fixed then deduct discount amount from the billing)
5. Generate a UI for this calculator for manual testing
6. Generate unit test for this 


for (BigDecimal quantity : Quantity){
    if(quantity < 10)
    {
        amount = unitprice * quantityPriceForQ1;
    }else if (quantity > 10 && quanity < 40){
        amount = unitprice * quantityPriceForQ2;
    }else if (quantity > 50){
        amount = unitprice * quantityPriceForQ3;
    }

}